cff-version: 1.2.0
title: The Protein Workbench
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Arijit
    family-names: Biswas
    affiliation: >-
      Institute of Experimental Hematology and Transfusion Medicine,
      University Hospital Bonn, Bonn, Germany
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4103-5854"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aribis77/protein-workbench"
url: "https://aribis77.github.io/protein-workbench/"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained browser-based workbench for structural interaction analysis,
  in-silico mutation and free energy calculation, in which every detected contact
  carries the evidence supporting it: real-space correlation against an experimental
  map, occupancy across an ensemble or trajectory, and predicted aligned error for
  predicted structures. That evidence is propagated into the downstream network,
  scanning and free energy results. Runs entirely client-side with no installation
  and no transmission of coordinates.
keywords:
  - structural biology
  - protein interaction networks
  - free energy calculation
  - cryo-EM validation
  - AlphaFold confidence
  - transglutaminase crosslinking
